<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Release network policy: encrypted traffic only.

    `android:usesCleartextTraffic="true"` used to sit in this manifest, which
    applies to every build type. It is what makes LAN development work against
    a laptop on http://192.168.x.x, and in a shipped app it meant SafeHer would
    accept plain HTTP from anyone able to answer for the host — quietly
    undoing the certificate pinning in `lib/core/network/`.

    For an app that carries a woman's live location and her recorded evidence,
    an attacker on the same cafe wifi reading or rewriting that traffic is the
    threat the pinning exists to stop.

    Cleartext now lives only in the debug and profile variants, which never
    reach a user.

    THE ONE EXCEPTION, added 2026-09-02: the SafeHer glasses.

    They serve MJPEG video over plain HTTP on the local network, because an
    ESP32-S3 cannot terminate TLS at 15 fps and there is no certificate
    authority that would issue for a device on someone's home wifi. Blocking it
    outright does not make the app safer -- it makes weapon detection fail
    silently in release builds while appearing wired, which is worse than the
    risk being managed.

    So cleartext is permitted for exactly one name, `safeher-glasses.local`,
    resolved over mDNS. That is narrow in a way a private-IP range would not be:
    the config cannot express CIDR, so permitting "the local network" would mean
    permitting cleartext to any host the user might type, which is how the
    blanket flag got here in the first place.

    What this does not weaken: the API base URL is https and pinned, and nothing
    about this entry applies to it. What crosses this link is video, and it
    never leaves the phone afterwards -- it is scored on the device and only a
    number is sent onward.
-->
<network-security-config>
    <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="false">
        <trust-anchors>
            <certificates src="system" />
        </trust-anchors>
    </base-config>

    <domain-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true">
        <domain includeSubdomains="true">safeher-glasses.local</domain>
    </domain-config>
</network-security-config>
